{
  "abstract": "Measurement is not taken to be a fundamental act, observer intervention, or separate kind of physics. It is an ordinary system-apparatus-environment process described with a retained record; discarding that record leaves a nonselective channel. This revision makes the data distinction exact in finite-dimensional quantum theory and states its consequence for Modal Triplet Theory. A pointer dephasing channel is completely positive and trace preserving, removes off-diagonal pointer blocks, and preserves pointer populations. The same nonselective channel is compatible with distinct outcome instruments having different probability laws, so the channel alone specifies neither records nor their probabilities. An MTT basin boundary or chart exit likewise does not choose a successor basin. A complete outcome-resolved model must provide an instrument or normalized continuation kernel and its source. The current canonical q79 binary recorder supplies an exact stopped-output law on its declared finite domain, while general apparatus contexts and objective single-history actualization remain open.",
